# ---------- Database ----------
# Leave DATABASE_URL unset for local dev: the app runs an embedded Postgres
# (PGlite) persisted in ./.pgdata, so there is nothing to install.
# Point it at real Postgres for staging/production. The schema is plain SQL and
# runs unchanged on Postgres 14+.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/loadboard

# ---------- Auth ----------
# 32+ random bytes. Sessions are signed with this; changing it logs everyone out.
# REQUIRED in production: the app refuses to start without it.
SESSION_SECRET=dev-only-secret-change-me-to-32-plus-random-bytes

# ---------- Demo mode ----------
# One-click sign-in on /login and inside the contact gate ("Sign in as demo
# driver"). It is an intentional authentication bypass and only makes sense on
# sample data -- set it to off the day real data goes in, and note that it is ON
# whenever this variable is unset. The board stays public either way; only the
# sign-in shortcut disappears, leaving the email/password form and self-serve
# /register.
DEMO_MODE=on

# ---------- Job extraction ----------
# Nothing to configure. Extraction is deterministic rules (src/lib/extract/),
# so it costs nothing to run, needs no network, and produces the same output
# for the same input. Tune it by editing the rules and running `npm run eval`
# and `npm run score`.

# ---------- WhatsApp Cloud API (Meta) ----------
# From Meta App Dashboard -> WhatsApp -> Configuration.
# WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN is the string you type into the webhook setup form.
# WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET signs the X-Hub-Signature-256 header we verify.
WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=dev-verify-token
# WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=
# Set to 1 to accept unsigned webhook posts (local testing only, never in prod).
WHATSAPP_ALLOW_UNSIGNED=1

# ---------- HERE Location Services ----------
# Powers the location type-ahead, address-level geocoding, reverse geocoding for
# "Use GPS", and TRUCK road distance / drive time on a job. Server-side only --
# never exposed to the browser. Without it the app falls back to the offline
# gazetteer and straight-line distance, and every screen still works.
# HERE_API_KEY=

# Billable HERE calls allowed per UTC day. The place routes are public (the
# board needs no account), so this caps what a script can spend on your invoice.
# Past the budget the app degrades to the offline gazetteer silently.
HERE_DAILY_BUDGET=2000

# ---------- Geocoding provider ----------
# Defaults to "here" when HERE_API_KEY is set, otherwise "local".
# local   -> offline gazetteer only (no network, no key)
# here    -> HERE Geocoding & Search
# census  -> US Census Bureau geocoder, free and keyless
# mapbox  -> Mapbox Geocoding v6, needs MAPBOX_TOKEN
# GEOCODER=local
# MAPBOX_TOKEN=

# ---------- Timezone ----------
# Relative dates ("tomorrow") are resolved against the sender's local day.
# LOAD_TZ=America/New_York

# ---------- Cron ----------
# Bearer token required by POST /api/cron/* (queue drain, expiry sweep, match
# sweep). Only an EXTERNAL scheduler needs it: the in-process scheduler below
# calls the sweep functions directly and never makes an HTTP request to itself.
CRON_SECRET=dev-cron-secret

# Whether THIS process runs the three sweeps on timers of its own, started from
# src/instrumentation.ts. Three states:
#
#   unset  -> on when NODE_ENV=production, off everywhere else. This is the
#             deployed default: production sweeps, laptops do not.
#   off    -> never. Set this on the task definition the day an EventBridge
#             Scheduler is created, and point it at the three POST routes with
#             the CRON_SECRET above. Nothing else changes; see infra/README.md.
#   on     -> always, including locally. `CRON_IN_PROCESS=on npm run dev` is how
#             you watch the sweeps fire against ./.pgdata.
#
# The cadences are constants, not variables: PROCESS_EVERY_MS (60 s),
# MATCH_EVERY_MS (3 min) and EXPIRE_EVERY_MS (1 h) in src/lib/cron/config.ts,
# which is also where the reasoning for each one is written down.
# CRON_IN_PROCESS=on
